The transcriptions, corrections, notes and other files in this repository are
licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
(CC BY 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

You may share and adapt them for any purpose, provided you give appropriate
credit. Please cite this dataset and, for any value you use, the original
record it cites (SOURCES.yml lists every source and its own terms).

The original records are not covered by this licence; SOURCES.yml gives each
source's own terms (`rights`). In outline:

- Records of the U.S. government (the National Archives' war patrol reports, war
  diaries, morning reports, muster rolls, Missing Air Crew Reports and films; the
  Library of Congress's situation maps; the wartime manuals and recognition
  plates) are in the public domain.
- Japanese records are read at the Japan Center for Asian Historical Records
  (JACAR): free to view, cited by reference code.
- British records (The National Archives, Kew) are Crown copyright; French and
  Italian newspapers and records are linked at the libraries that hold them.
- Items from the 45th Infantry Division Museum require the credit line given in
  SOURCES.yml.
- The FRUPAC war maps (CC BY-NC-ND) and films on archives' YouTube channels are
  linked, never copied.
- Weather is ERA5 (Copernicus, CC BY 4.0, through Open-Meteo); place coordinates
  are from OpenStreetMap Nominatim (ODbL 1.0).

One exception to CC BY 4.0 among this repository's own files: the P.108B
silhouette in silhouettes/silhouettes.yml is adapted from a CC BY-SA 3.0 drawing
(Kaboldy, Wikimedia Commons) and carries that licence and attribution.
